  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"48\" data-end=\"327\">The <strong data-start=\"52\" data-end=\"77\">Histone Antibody test</strong> detects <strong data-start=\"86\" data-end=\"104\">autoantibodies</strong> against <strong data-start=\"113\" data-end=\"133\">histone proteins</strong>, which are key components of cell nuclei. This test is most commonly used to evaluate for <strong data-start=\"224\" data-end=\"267\">drug-induced lupus erythematosus (DILE)</strong>, but it may also be positive in other autoimmune disorders.</p>\n<p data-start=\"48\" data-end=\"327\">Positive results are most commonly associated with:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"947\" data-end=\"1561\">\n<li data-start=\"947\" data-end=\"1044\">\n<p data-start=\"949\" data-end=\"1044\"><strong data-start=\"949\" data-end=\"992\">Drug-induced lupus erythematosus (DILE)</strong> (e.g., from hydralazine, procainamide, isoniazid)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1045\" data-end=\"1107\">\n<p data-start=\"1047\" data-end=\"1107\">May also be seen in <strong data-start=\"1067\" data-end=\"1105\">systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1108\" data-end=\"1561\">\n<p data-start=\"1110\" data-end=\"1561\">Occasionally positive in <strong data-start=\"1135\" data-end=\"1159\">rheumatoid arthritis</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1161\" data-end=\"1176\">scleroderma</strong>, or other autoimmune conditions<br data-start=\"1208\" data-end=\"1211\">Further evaluation with <strong data-start=\"1235\" data-end=\"1250\">ANA pattern</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1252\" data-end=\"1266\">anti-dsDNA</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"1272\" data-end=\"1292\">clinical history</strong> is needed. |<br>| <strong data-start=\"1308\" data-end=\"1320\">Negative</strong> | No detectable anti-histone antibodies.<br data-start=\"1371\" data-end=\"1374\">Makes <strong data-start=\"1380\" data-end=\"1402\">drug-induced lupus</strong> less likely, but <strong data-start=\"1420\" data-end=\"1441\">does not rule out</strong> idiopathic SLE or other autoimmune diseases.<br data-start=\"1486\" data-end=\"1489\">Consider other markers (e.g., ANA, anti-dsDNA, anti-Smith antibodies).&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Histone Antibodies</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Notes</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Drug-induced lupus</td>\n<td>Frequently Positive</td>\n<td>Typically resolves after stopping the drug</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Idiopathic SLE</td>\n<td>May be Positive</td>\n<td>Often along with other antibodies (anti-dsDNA, anti-Sm)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Other autoimmune diseases</td>\n<td>Occasionally Positive</td>\n<td>Non-specific; seen in a small % of cases</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
